# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Never commit secrets
*.key
secrets.*

# Prebuilt APK for direct install (tracked on purpose)
!/apk/*.apk

# Signing material: normally never committed, with ONE deliberate exception.
#
# keystore/release.jks IS tracked. A sideloaded app can only be updated over an
# existing install if the signature matches, and the CI builds used to fall back
# to the debug key — which GitHub regenerates on every fresh runner, so every
# release was signed differently and could not be installed over the previous
# one. Committing a fixed keystore is what makes in-place updates possible.
#
# This is not a secret in any meaningful sense (its password is in
# app/build.gradle.kts in plain sight); it provides signature stability, not
# protection. Replace it with your own if you fork this.
*.jks
*.keystore
keystore.properties
!keystore/release.jks
